## GovernanceTests.fs is model-agnostic; BehaviorTests.fs carries the model behavior

References to the product model API (`Product.Program.view/update/generatedHost`,
`controlsExampleView`, `adapterProgram`, `dispatchViewerKey`, `Product.Model`):

    GovernanceTests.fs : 0   (reads SOURCE TEXT only — productSource/productSources, build.fsx scans)
    BehaviorTests.fs   : 13  (calls the scaffold view/update/host/scene-text directly)

## Conclusion (SC-003)

Swapping the scaffold model (`src/FrictionCheck/Model.fs` etc.) changes only the model API
that `BehaviorTests.fs` calls, so only `BehaviorTests.fs` needs rewriting. `GovernanceTests.fs`
exercises no model API — it asserts source/structure/evidence-discoverability invariants over
file text — so it keeps compiling and passing across the model swap. The compile order
guarantees the durable governance unit is independent of the replaceable behavior unit.

The model-agnosticism is enforced at the repo level by the durable/replaceable separation in
`template/base/tests/Product.Tests/{GovernanceTests,BehaviorTests}.fs` and by
`Governance.Tests` (ControlsBoundaryCompositionTests -> BehaviorTests.fs;
GeneratedGuidanceTests/AsteroidsFeedbackSkillGuidanceTests repointed to the correct half).
